details:
(a) whether Government has undertaken any measures to promote sustainable tourism and address the challenges arising from increasing tourist footfall at popular destinations;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the initiatives undertaken to encourage diversification of tourism through niche tourism products and development of lesser-known destinations;
(d) whether any institutional framework has been established for promoting environmentally sustainable tourism practices, community participation and responsible visitor management at tourism destinations; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has conducted any review of the implementation of''Ek Ped Maa Ke Naam'' campaign;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of measures taken to strengthen public participation, institutional support and community involvement under the campaign;
(d) whether any mechanism has been established for digital monitoring, survival assessment and long-term maintenance of plantations carried out through the campaign; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether steps have been taken to broaden investment opportunities in highway infrastructure and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether the Ministry has initiated any measure to encourage private investment in the development of National Highways, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether the concession framework governing Public-Private Partnership (PPP) projects has been amended to promote private investment in the development of National Highways, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the status of the implementation of digital toll collection initiatives on the National Highways;
(b) the information regarding measures undertaken to facilitate technology-enabled toll collection on the National Highway network;
(c) whether the Ministry is planning to expand barrier-free electronic toll collection; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of Bharat Taxi, operated by Sahakar Taxi Cooperative Limited, including the number of registered drivers and customers, as on date;
(b) the cities in which the service is currently operational and the details of its proposed expansion to other cities, including the timeline for reaching 500 cities;
(c) the manner in which the driver-owned cooperative model is expected to ensure better earnings and welfare for drivers as compared to existing app-based ride-hailing platforms; and
(d) whether any regulatory or financial support has been extended by Government for the expansion of this initiative?

(a) the details of the guidelines used in selecting heavy industry clusters for deployment of carbon mitigation systems under the newly announced ?20,000 crore CCUS Technology Fund;
(b) whether Government has established a specific emissions-reduction audit framework to assess the efficiency of carbon capture in selected pilot thermal power plants;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government proposes to issue standardized rules to enable Municipal Corporations to issue green bonds for the rejuvenation of urban wetlands; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of Central and State Government services currently available through UMANG and DigiLocker platforms;
(b) the total number of users on these platforms and transactions carried out during the last three years; and
(c) the measures taken by Government to improve digital access and service delivery in rural and remote areas?

(a) the total number of accounts opened under Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) till date;
(b) the State/UT-wise number of PMJDY Account holders as of May 2026;
(c) whether any facilities are being provided to the PMJDY Account holders, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether there are any minimum balance charges for the PMJDY Account holders, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the number of women Jan Dhan Account holders?

(a) the number of railway stations where redevelopment has been completed so far under the Amrit Bharat Station Scheme (ABSS) and the number of stations where redevelopment works are in progress;
(b) the passenger amenities and modernisation works completed so far at these stations;
(c) the details of the stations selected under the Scheme, State-wise; and
(d) the total investment made so far and the timeline for completion of the remaining works?

(a) the number of Vande Bharat train services currently in operation and the number of new train services that are proposed to be introduced during the year 2026-27 in the country including Uttarkhand;
(b) the progress made so far of the Mumbai-Ahmedabad Bullet Train Project and by when it is planned to be launched;
(c) status of plans to develop a Delhi-Siliguri high speed line; 
(d) the steps taken to promote the indigenous manufacturing of rolling stock for high-speed trains; and
(e) the impact of these initiatives on passengers' travel time and railway revenue?

(a) whether Government has introduced reforms to make passport services more accessible, efficient and citizen-centric and if so, the salient features thereof;
(b) the present status of implementation of e-Passports, including coverage achieved and the roadmap for phased expansion;
(c) whether steps have been taken to strengthen the network and service delivery of Passport Seva Kendras and Post Office Passport Seva Kendras, particularly in underserved areas; and
(d) the details of digital and technological interventions adopted to improve transparency, reduce processing time and enhance the overall passport service experience?

(a) the district-wise target for survey and physical registration of ancient scripts under the newly structured Gyan Bharatam Mission framework;
(b) whether the Ministry has integrated advanced Optical Character Recognition (OCR) technology on its portal to process the 18 crore newly digitised manuscript pages, and;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) how the Ministry plans to resolve copy-ownership and intellectual property challenges while allowing open public research access to rare religious manuscripts?

(a) the current status of ongoing nuclear energy projects in the country; 
(b) the details of recent developments in the commissioning and operation of indigenous nuclear reactors, including the Prototype Fast Breeder Reactor (PFBR); 
(c) the operational performance of Nuclear Power Corporation of India Limited (NPCIL) during the last year; and
(d) the details of major collaborations and initiatives undertaken to strengthen nuclear power generation in the country?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of progress achieved under the Smart Cities Mission (SCM), particularly with regard to completion of projects relating to urban mobility, Integrated Command and Control Centres (ICCCs), water supply and waste management;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to replicate the best practices and technology solutions developed under the SCM in other urban local bodies and cities across the country to strengthen urban governance and service delivery; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the progress made under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana–Urban (PMAY-U) towards achieving the objective of ‘Housing for All’ in urban areas, particularly with regard to the number of houses sanctioned, completed and under construction across various States;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to continue or restructure the scheme beyond its present implementation period in order to address the remaining shortage of affordable housing in urban areas; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any comprehensive assessment of airport infrastructure capacity in view of the rapid growth of passenger traffic, (in FY 2025, Indian airports handled 412 million passengers and the same is projected to increase to 665 million by FY 2031);
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has prepared any long-term roadmap for expansion of the airport network in the country, particularly in view of the stated vision to increase the number of operational airports substantially in the coming decades; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of major schemes and programmes presently being implemented by the Central Government to promote tree plantation in the country for environmental protection and enhancement of green cover;
(b) whether mechanisms have been established to assess and monitor the survival rate of planted saplings; and
(c) whether Government is considering to develop any digital/online tracking system to ensure the effectiveness and transparency of tree plantation programmes?

(a) whether Government is implementing any special plan or guidelines for conservation of Khandagiri–Udaygiri Jain religious site and for integrated management of facilities for devotees, that houses ancient Jain idols and religious activities;
(b) whether Government is considering to provide free or separate entry arrangements for Jain devotees in the temple area; and
(c) whether any proposal is under consideration for overall development of the site, keeping in view its religious significance and its potential for pilgrimage tourism and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is going to introduce any new scheme for the conservation of trees and increasing forest area, if so, the details of the new scheme and until when it would be implemented; 
(b) whether Government is monitoring the tree plantation done on special occasions, if so, the number of trees planted during last five years along with the number of trees surviving out of that; and
(c) whether Government is considering to implement any mandatory rule for tree plantation while according approval to building construction map, if not, whether any such plan is in the offing?

(a) the number of Ayurvedic and Homeopathic Research Centres set up by Government during the last three years;
(b) whether adequate funds have been allocated for setting up these centres and if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise;
(c) whether Government has received any proposal for allocation of additional funds and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the other steps taken by Government to promote research and development in Homeopathy in the country?

(a) the specific results achieved during the "Special Campaign 3.0" aimed at reducing public grievances and improving sanitation;
(b) the number of public grievances resolved along with action taken in respect of pending references from Members of Parliament, PMO and Parliament; and
(c) the good practices adopted under the Swachhata Abhiyaan particularly at the Regional Offices of the Ministry?

(a) the details of Nagar Van Yojana approved under the Ministry’s 100 days action plan in Jharkhand and all States and Union Territories;
(b) the target of tree plantation by 2025 under Nagar Van Yojana and the progress made so far; and
(c) whether Nagar Van Yojana is helpful in protecting urban areas from environmental degradation and encroachment?

(a) the aims and objectives of the new school safety guidelines to ensure safety of students in both private and Government schools;
(b) the details of safety concerns addressed by the guidelines; and
(c) the efforts made by the Ministry for the implementation of the guidelines in the States including the State of Uttar Pradesh?
